	This is due to the global $w$ upper bound ($\approx$ 399.37) being much larger than the local $w$ upper bound  ($\approx$ 0.30) near $x = 0.25$. In this case, enforcing a global constraint $w \le w_{\max}$ can no longer help mitigate the $v$-overshoot in the vicinity.

