		\quad
		w^{(r)}(x,0) = 0.5,\; r = 1, 2, 3, 4.
	\end{gather*}
	The traffic flow entering the junction from incoming Road 1 is equally distributed among outgoing Roads 2--4.
	The BP-OEDG scheme is used to solve this problem with $\gamma = 0$ and $\gamma = 2$, respectively. The obtained numerical results are presented in \Cref{fig:T5}. As one can see, the wave structures are sharply resolved, and they match well with the results reported in \cite{buli2020discontinuous,canic2015runge}.

